      "user_input": "params[:path].to_s",
      "confidence": "Weak",
      "cwe_id": [22],
      "note": "By design: Bookwall is a single-user self-hosted app and this endpoint exists to expose the server's filesystem to the only operator (authenticated via session cookie) so they can pick a library root from the UI. Only directory listings are returned (never file contents), the response is read-only (no write paths), and the rails process can only enumerate what its uid can already read. Path traversal isn't meaningful since the input is an absolute path the user supplies directly."
